### Exercise 9.1

NOT COMPLETE!

The dataset \href{https://github.com/mattiasvillani/BayesianLearningBook/raw/main/data/bivar_missing.csv}{bivarmissing.csv} contains $n = 20$ observations
on the two variables $X_1$ and $X_2$. Note that four observations are missing in the dataset (coded with NA).
Assume the bivariate normal model for the data: $\mathbf{x}_1,...,\mathbf{x}_n \vert \boldsymbol{\theta}, \boldsymbol{\Sigma} \overset{iid}{\sim}\mathrm{N}(\boldsymbol{\theta},\boldsymbol{\Sigma})$, with mean vector $\boldsymbol{\theta} = (\theta_1,\theta_2)^\top$ and covariance matrix $\boldsymbol{\Sigma}$.

